3. Simulation loop expansion
This is the engine’s heartbeat.
State representation:
{
  "time": 0.0,
  "isotopes": [...],
  "environment": {...}
}
Core loop (conceptual):
Evaluate current state
For each isotope:
call K(Z, N, E, S)
get (S_{\text{stab}}, E_b, \mathcal{D}, \mathcal{F})
Determine transitions
for unstable isotopes, sample or choose decay modes from (\mathcal{D})
apply decay rules → generate new isotopes
Update environment (optional)
if scenario includes dynamic environment, update (\vec{E})
Advance time
t = t + Δt
Record snapshot
append state to timeline in scenario/blueprint
Termination conditions
no more unstable isotopes
time limit reached
energy budget exhausted
user-defined condition met
Pseudo-structure:
state = init_state()
while not done(state):
    state = evaluate_and_transition(state)
    record(state)
The important part: all transitions are kernel-derived, not arbitrary.

